# Example ReRDMFT input file: LiH, 6-31G, GNOF, FULL_OPTIMIZATION TRUE with ORBITAL_OPTIMIZER
# NEO -- the NEO counterpart of lih_gnof_c4_full_optimization.inp, same system, same functional,
# including C4_SPINOR. See that file's own header comment for why C4_DHF's orbital rotations are
# restricted to the positive-energy spinors only (turning what would otherwise be a min-max
# saddle-point search into an ordinary minimization). Because of that restriction, NEO's default
# target_order = 0 is the physically correct target here too: watch for the post-loop
# "[PASS] the point is a genuine minimum (0 negative eigenvalues)" on the C4_DHF section, exactly
# like the X2C section right above it. Compare its converged energy against
# lih_gnof_c4_full_optimization.inp's own ADAM result as a routine cross-check (they agree to
# ~1e-9 Hartree here).
NELEC 4
BASIS lih-6-31g.gbs
NON_RELATIVISTIC TRUE
X2C TRUE
C4_SPINOR TRUE
FUNCTIONAL GNOF
PNOF_SUBSPACES 2
PNOF_COUPLING 2
FULL_OPTIMIZATION TRUE
ORBITAL_OPTIMIZER NEO

GEOMETRY
Li  0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
H   0.000000   0.000000   1.594900
END
